Algorithm replacement diff
==========================
Old: best.pt/Ultralytics frame classifier returned normal/unnormal and confidence.
New: Go MatchHTML(source, threshold) evaluates the supplied reference signals:
  js_trig_leg_animation 20, defs_use_reuse 15, reduced_motion_js 12,
  play_pause_button 12, title_desc_aria_labelledby 10,
  visibilitychange_listener 8, multiword_kebab_naming 8,
  no_root_css_vars 7, pure_svg_scene 8.
The score is round(100*raw_points/100, 1), with matched/missing signal names and
version code-fingerprint-v1. Default threshold is 55. Model A is normal by
default; an administrator may select the inverse normal class.

The HTML/SVG source is graded before browser preview rendering. The frontend
renders bounded preview_html in an iframe with sandbox="allow-scripts" and a
strict CSP. Historical PNG/WebP records remain readable. The backend image no
longer installs or invokes Chromium, Python or Playwright; no new renderer URL
or Compose setting is introduced.

OAuth scope follow-up
=====================
qualityProbeSupported now requires AccountTypeOAuth exactly. Active OpenAI/Gemini
OAuth accounts remain eligible (subject to source/degraded group routing); API-key
and service-account accounts return false before any probe request is scheduled.
